03_TRD.docx (paragraph 79; policy_64b427692eb932980612b66d): The assembler returns required_evidence_ids, attached_evidence_ids and missing_evidence_ids for the selected candidate, together with dependency_manifest_version and dependency_review_status. missing_evidence_ids is the required set minus the attached set. Coverage is complete only when the dependency manifest is approved for the exact manual checksum, the action evidence is present, all required objects are attached, and their content and provenance pass extraction checks. An empty or unreviewed required set cannot establish sufficiency. Finding a table object is insufficient if its required headers, units or variant context are missing.
03_TRD.docx (paragraph 80; policy_92d58d1828c67f67c189cfe8): Perform the existing bounded recovery search for missing dependencies and record its outcome. A source gap that the rider cannot resolve must block the instruction and enter source review or abstention; do not ask the rider to supply a missing manual warning or table header. Retrieval outages, invalid index objects and other operational failures return SYSTEM_ERROR. Cross-encoder scores rank relevance and cannot approve a dependency manifest, infer a diagnostic order or waive missing evidence.
